 "description": {
  "lang": "en",
  "script": "Latn",
  "text": "Unanchored, But Not Lost a book by Selam Fessha What happens when the life you built no longer feels like home? Unanchored, But Not Lost is a deeply personal and transformative journey through burnout, motherhood, identity loss, financial anxiety, and the quiet unraveling that many women experience—but few dare to name. At her lowest point, during a season marked by emotional exhaustion and uncertainty, the author was asked a terrifying question by her therapist: Who are you when everything you were anchored to is gone? That question became the beginning of healing."
 },
